[2026-06-24T11:17:53.196Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_496","type":"reasoning","text":"**Monitoring current runs**\n\nI need to watch the current runs, so I think I can use `gh run watch` in background sessions. Monitoring seems essential, and using `exec` with it might work, though the default timeout is only 2 minutes. I wonder if the session yields if it’s still running after that. If ongoing, the `exec_command` should return a session ID. Running two watchers with output to logs might be helpful. Maybe I should consider not using a timeout and set the yield time to 1000?"}}
